# Sequence 00 — The First Line

The universe begins as a single golden drafting line in total darkness.  
This line becomes the first coordinate of the Blueprint Grid.

The grid assembles itself cell by cell, revealing the Pong Microcell —  
the first simulation arena, the first atom, the first loop.

This sequence establishes the recursive visual language of the Blueprint Universe.

# Sequence 01 — The Architect’s Entrance

A cosmic figure materialises from geometry.  
The Architect awakens the Seed of Reality, activating the Codex Layer.

Blueprint glyphs orbit the Architect like a cosmic UI.  
The universe responds to their gestures, aligning itself into order.

This sequence introduces the governing intelligence of the Blueprint Universe.

# Sequence 02 — The Realm Map Reveal

Five elemental realms ignite along the Cosmic Meridian:

- Air  
- Water  
- Earth  
- Fire  
- Storm  

They form the Cosmic Tree — a vertical stack of worlds connected by golden lines.

This sequence reveals the macro‑scale architecture of the universe.

# Sequence 02.5 — The First Simulation Cell (PONG-Earth)

Earth appears as the ball in a cosmic Pong arena.  
Two paddles — Order (cyan) and Chaos (red) — volley it across the Blueprint Grid.

Symbolism:
- Earth = the first stable node of Manifestation  
- Paddles = opposing cosmic forces  
- Grid = the OS substrate  
- Motion = harmonic cycles of creation  

This is the first interactive moment in the Blueprint Universe.

# Sequence 03 — The Codex Awakening

The Codex Layer activates.  
Glyphs, runes, and blueprint symbols assemble into a living manuscript.

The Architect reveals the hidden logic of the universe —  
the laws, constants, and frequencies that govern all realms.

This sequence introduces the linguistic and symbolic layer of reality.

# Sequence 04 — Avatar Selection Chamber

A chamber of floating silhouettes, each representing a potential avatar:

- The Navigator  
- The Sentinel  
- The Sovereign  
- The Ronin  
- The Scribe  

The viewer chooses their form.  
The chamber responds with light, geometry, and resonance.

This sequence bridges cinematic narrative and player identity.
